{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a movie that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the film is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his quick wit and sharp dialogue. the movie follows mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as he navigates the complexities of creating a social networking site while attending harvard university.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard, being dumped by his girlfriend erica albright, played by rooney mara. this event sets off a chain reaction that leads mark to create a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes incredibly popular, but also generates a lot of controversy and attention from the university administration.\n\nmark's success with facemash catches the attention of twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss, played by armie hammer, who approach him with an idea for a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark agrees to work on the site, but eventually drops the twins and launches his own site, thefacebook, with the help of his friend eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield.\n\nas thefacebook gains popularity, mark becomes increasingly obsessed with the site and begins to push away his friends and acquaintances. the site expands to other colleges and universities, and mark becomes a celebrity of sorts, but he also faces lawsuits from the winklevoss twins and eduardo saverin, who claim that mark stole their ideas and cheated them out of their rightful share of the company.\n\nthe movie is full of clever dialogue and witty one-liners, and the cast delivers strong performances across the board. jesse eisenberg is particularly impressive as mark zuckerberg, bringing a sense of vulnerability and intensity to the role. the film also features a great soundtrack, with a score by trent reznor and atticus ross that adds to the movie's tension and energy.\n\none of the most interesting aspects of the social network is its portrayal of the darker side of success and ambition. mark zuckerberg is a complex and often unlikeable character, and the film doesn't shy away from showing his flaws and mistakes. at the same time, the movie also celebrates the creativity and innovation that went into creating facebook, and the ways in which the site has changed the way we communicate and interact with each other.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking movie that explores the complexities of success, ambition, and friendship. it's a film that will resonate with anyone who has ever struggled with the challenges of creating something new and innovative, and the consequences that can follow when you achieve your goals.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0028338772244751453}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0297507643699646}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.005243951920419931}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -1.0614714622497559}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00018165845540352166}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.19502811133861542}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.10389747470617294}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.011228349059820175}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -5.8530047681415454e-05}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.825939416885376}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -2.7418097943154862e-06}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.4507860839366913}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.623152494430542}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00026127262390218675}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0012